commit-response-output-after-success

Lane: cross

Unit: commit-model-output-after-successful-response

ChildPatch: commit-response-output-after-success

Form: GitDiff

Segment: snapshot

Purpose: Publish complete successful model responses without exposing failed or interrupted buffered output.

Requires: Unit:cross/track-model-responses-by-attempt, Unit:mixed/recover-websocket-requests-without-http-fallback

Provides: Buffer native model-output events on Plus, Pro and ProLite ChatGPT WebSocket requests until the original successful terminal. Preserve immediate controls and native event order, discard failed and interrupted output, retain reported interruption usage as spending without replacing installed context or admitting incremental continuation, and activate the existing 300-second content-progress deadline independently of observation. Preserve usage at sampling, foreground compaction and memory consumers.

Boundary: Response recording and receipt progress remain with track-model-responses-by-attempt; WebSocket RTT remains independent. Preserve native authentication, retries, input steering, hard cancellation, interruption acknowledgement validation and completion retention while draining. Ordinary incomplete responses retain their original errors and usage payloads. Background compaction retains its native HTTP and budget-only accounting. HTTP, API-key and other non-admitted paths retain streaming behavior. Do not add storage, pricing, presentation controls or observer-dependent output admission.

Verification: Complete-response API tests cover successful commit, transport and protocol failure, incomplete usage, interruption and content deadlines with and without observation. Account-scope, prewarm ordering, interrupted-continuation and real input-steering tests verify output admission, spending-only context accounting and completion winning an interrupt race. Foreground compaction tests preserve reported interruption spending without installing discarded output, and native background tests retain accounting isolation. HTTP absence and native cancellation tests preserve streaming and completion draining; retry tests retain progress-timeout retries without the connection-cycle wait. Real Plus WebSocket core tests flush and parse rollout JSONL after completed and incomplete responses with and without a terminal response ID, verifying exactly-once reported spending, unchanged installed context, and absence of discarded output from UI events and conversation storage.

CrossGroup: control-center


